not a uniform numerical lower bound over all words.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-visibility"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.visibility","kind":"claim","label":"Finite visibility choices precede the small-packet limit","locator":"05-seed-simulation.tex:875–974; lem:seed-huge-transverse and eq:seed-formal-visibility","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-seed","statement":"Huge transverse insertions are weakly zero against bounded tail families. Each of the finitely many required visibility functions is analytic in the seeded word angles and has a common nonzero test value at zero angles, 4bz exp(−8b²). A small generic perturbation avoids all required zeros and zero echo times. Finite selective lists are then chosen successively using earlier limiting data, before r is chosen.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.visibility","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.seed_removal","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.seed_removal%22%2C%22circuit.visibility%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.seed_removal%22%2C%22circuit.visibility%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.visibility"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.visibility","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.visibility%22%2C%22circuit.seed_packets%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%2